# A function definition with a redirect on its body: `f() { cat; } >out`. The
# redirect attaches to the body CompoundCommand (POSIX §2.9.4 redirect_list),
# which the function body carries for free.
<<<cmd
printf 'f() { cat; } >out\n' | "$PP" run std.shell --input - --dump-tree
<<<assert
exit 0
out-absent ERROR
out-absent MISSING
out-contains FunctionDefinition
out-contains body: CompoundCommand
out-count 1 redirect: Redirect
